~ intro
Señor Food: So, it's your first day? Welcome to my restaurant. Let me tell you a little about myself.
Señor Food: A few years ago I was let go from Google. Ay, qué desastre. It was devastating.
Señor Food: So I started cooking. And I realized I was pretty good. 
Señor Food: While I cook, I feel in my element. Es una cosa hermosa. So naturally, I decided to share my gift with the world, hence my restaurant.
Señor Food: Cooking has become a way of expression for me. And what better way to express myself than to automate it?! 
Señor Food: In my free time I've created a couple robots to help me around the shop. The people of San Jose love it.
Señor Food: The robots are not very advanced though. So I need your help.
Señor Food: I need training data for my robots. And you have, what, 2 years of experience at Chick Fil A? Perfecto, more than enough.
Señor Food: Do your thing, running the restaurant, and I'll have your every move tracked.
Señor Food: Then I'll feed this training data to my bots.
Señor Food: I hear this is a common practice at Meta: hire people to train their replacements! Genius, ¿no?
Señor Food: Just think of it this way, we are pushing the culinary frontier with the latest advancements in technology. 
Señor Food: Bueno, ya. Enough talking, get to work!
=> END


# STORY SCAFFOLD
# These titles are intentionally passive: no player responses or branches.
# Call each title once when its noted gameplay milestone happens. The TODO
# lines are writing prompts, not finished dialogue, so the final voice can be
# written in place without changing the progression structure.


## Beat 1 — First proof the restaurant can earn money.
## Trigger: after the first completed order / first positive money change.
## Story job: establish that Señor Food still thinks about success in startup terms.
~ story_first_earnings
Señor Food: TODO — FIRST EARNINGS: a short observation about the first dollars coming in; connect the small rush of a successful order to shipping or launching something in Silicon Valley.
=> END


## Beat 2 — The kitchen stops being just a starter setup.
## Trigger: after buying the first non-starter ingredient crate or Counter.
## Story job: show him taking genuine pleasure in expanding what can be cooked,
## while framing it with product/scale language he has not shaken.
~ story_first_upgrade
Señor Food: TODO — FIRST UPGRADE: notice the new ingredient or workspace; let cooking excitement and old tech-job instincts sit side by side.
=> END


## Beat 3 — Washing and fresh prep make the work feel tactile again.
## Trigger: after purchasing and placing the Sink.
## Story job: contrast physical, sensory kitchen work with the abstraction of his old job.
~ story_sink
Señor Food: TODO — SINK: a brief reflection on touching, washing, or preparing real ingredients; suggest that this is what he did not know he missed.
=> END


## Beat 4 — Cold storage brings back the comforts and compromises of an office kitchen.
## Trigger: after purchasing and placing the Fridge.
## Story job: bring Silicon Valley into the foreground: office perks, colleagues,
## routine, or belonging. Do not resolve his conflict yet.
~ story_fridge
Señor Food: TODO — FRIDGE: a memory of the old workplace prompted by this appliance; acknowledge that he misses more than the paycheck.
=> END


## Beat 5 — The oven lets him make something slower and more deliberate.
## Trigger: after purchasing and placing the Oven.
## Story job: pivot toward cooking as craft; he should recognize that his former
## job also gave him purpose, pressure, and a sense of making things with others.
~ story_oven
Señor Food: TODO — OVEN: reflect on waiting, timing, and care; put the satisfaction of cooking beside the parts of Silicon Valley he still misses.
=> END


## Beat 6 — His own automation plan starts to resemble the work he lost.
## Trigger: after the first recipe becomes automatable or the first bot is dispatched.
## Story job: make the tension explicit: automation is exciting, but it echoes
## the job and replacement anxiety introduced in the opening.
~ story_first_automation
Señor Food: TODO — AUTOMATION: react to the robot handling learned work; leave him proud, uneasy, and reminded of the team or work he used to have.
=> END


## Beat 7 — End after the game's most involved current recipe: Garden Veggie Burger.
## Trigger: the first time RecipeTracker records the `veggie_burger` recipe.
## Story job: close on recognition rather than a decision. Señor Food sees a
## complicated meal come together and understands he misses cooking and Silicon
## Valley at the same time. Leave the future open.
~ story_final_veggie_burger
Señor Food: TODO — FINAL VEGGIE BURGER: witness the finished six-step dish; land on a quiet, unresolved realization that both kitchens—the restaurant and his old career—matter to him.
=> END
